WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:04.920
Helck and his little brother Cless
became orphans at a young age

00:04.920 --> 00:07.040
after their parents were killed by monsters.

00:07.040 --> 00:11.000
As they lived in poverty and faced
constant harassment by members of nobility,

00:11.000 --> 00:13.290
Helck worked hard to keep Cless safe.

00:13.290 --> 00:17.000
Over the years,
Cless grew into a steadfast hero,

00:17.000 --> 00:18.830
and eventually had to leave the capital

00:18.830 --> 00:22.290
after being tasked with leading
a monster hunting expedition.

00:22.750 --> 00:26.500
When I get back, I'd really love to have
some of your home cooking.

00:26.500 --> 00:27.460
Roger that!

00:27.460 --> 00:30.210
Then you can count on one of my
special stamina-booster meals

00:30.210 --> 00:31.960
to be waiting on the table for you!

00:32.420 --> 00:34.040
Make sure you come back alive!

00:34.040 --> 00:35.000
Right!

00:54.500 --> 00:57.040
Aa, touzen mitai ni tsuyosa kazashite

00:57.040 --> 00:59.210
Noudo mashiteku rettoukanjou

00:59.210 --> 01:01.170
Umareta toki kara

01:01.170 --> 01:03.380
Kimatterutte oshietoite yo

01:03.380 --> 01:05.130
Risoukyou no otonari san

01:05.130 --> 01:07.330
Zetsubou ga sa hora "konnichiwa"

01:07.330 --> 01:09.380
Daremo kizukanai no wa

01:09.380 --> 01:11.540
Kou ka fukou ka?

01:11.540 --> 01:14.750
Nando mezamete mo

01:14.750 --> 01:17.880
Akumu no you dana

01:17.880 --> 01:21.250
Kurushii dake nara

01:21.580 --> 01:23.380
Kamisama douka boku o tsukurikaete kuranai ka

01:23.380 --> 01:27.290
Kamisama douka boku o tsukurikaete kuranai ka

01:27.290 --> 01:29.420
Aa, nanmannen mo bokura wa

01:29.420 --> 01:32.000
Mirai ni kibou idakinagara

01:32.000 --> 01:33.880
Douse otozureru ketsumatsu ni

01:33.880 --> 01:36.170
Aragou to surun da

01:36.170 --> 01:37.830
Nankai me no inori da

01:37.830 --> 01:40.170
Kokoro karada kawari hatete

01:40.170 --> 01:44.630
Magamono datte nan datte shinjitakute

01:44.750 --> 01:48.130
Are, boku wa ima ikiteru no?

01:48.130 --> 01:50.880
Mou wake wakannai ya

01:50.880 --> 01:52.880
Helck me tasukete yo

02:06.040 --> 02:10.960
<b>The Mercenaries</b>

02:11.420 --> 02:14.960
Only half a month after Cless departed
on his expedition,

02:16.130 --> 02:19.420
monsters began to appear
in greater numbers than ever before.

02:19.420 --> 02:23.630
And in order to combat them,
the kingdom enacted a military draft.

02:23.920 --> 02:26.670
Just like Cless, I was assigned
to a monster hunting squadron

02:26.670 --> 02:29.290
and had to leave the capital for some time.

02:32.790 --> 02:33.830
Retreat!

02:33.830 --> 02:35.170
Run for it!

02:37.040 --> 02:40.540
<b>Son of a Baron</b>

02:37.040 --> 02:40.540
<b>Edil</b>

02:38.540 --> 02:40.330
Hey, buddy! You gotta stand up!

02:43.830 --> 02:45.710
Come on! We're running for it!

02:46.130 --> 02:48.710
What the hell is this abomination?!

02:48.880 --> 02:53.670
The monster we encountered that day
was like nothing we had ever seen before.

02:54.170 --> 02:56.420
He must be talking about a New-World Lifeform!

02:56.540 --> 02:59.040
They sometimes appear in places
where the toxin is most potent.

02:59.040 --> 03:01.670
Although they look similar,
they're totally different from normal monsters!

03:02.750 --> 03:03.830
Now I see!

03:03.830 --> 03:06.130
This must be when Helck first encountered one!

03:06.130 --> 03:07.960
That thing was downright terrifying.

03:07.960 --> 03:10.580
I didn't even consider trying to fight it.

03:10.580 --> 03:13.170
All I wanted to do
was get the hell out of there.

03:13.500 --> 03:14.750
Understandable.

03:14.750 --> 03:18.670
The thought of fighting those creatures is
daunting even for our warriors in the Empire.

03:18.670 --> 03:21.460
But since some of my comrades were still alive,

03:21.460 --> 03:23.790
I couldn't just escape and leave them
to fend for themselves.

03:24.710 --> 03:28.290
So I faced off against the monster,
knowing full well that it might kill me.

03:28.580 --> 03:29.920
How foolhardy.

03:31.380 --> 03:34.330
The monster packed a punch that was
far stronger than anything I had imagined.

03:34.330 --> 03:35.380
It really hurt.

03:35.380 --> 03:37.880
All it took was one blow
to nearly knock me unconscious.

03:39.630 --> 03:40.880
Hurry and get out of here!

03:45.040 --> 03:47.540
He's actually holding his own
against that monstrosity!

03:47.540 --> 03:50.130
I was only trying to buy enough time
for everyone else to run away.

03:50.130 --> 03:52.460
So I focused on bearing the brunt
of its attacks for as long as I could.

03:53.500 --> 03:55.290
Then it suddenly hit me.

03:56.460 --> 03:58.630
I was holding up better than I expected to.

03:59.210 --> 04:01.830
So I decided to change gears
and try counterattacking.

04:03.420 --> 04:04.420
It would strike me.

04:04.750 --> 04:05.920
And I would strike back.

04:06.170 --> 04:09.000
We exchanged blows over and over.

04:09.460 --> 04:12.170
I had no understanding
of how to fight properly.

04:12.170 --> 04:14.500
So I just kept haphazardly
throwing my fists at it.

04:15.790 --> 04:17.830
And eventually, I won.

04:18.670 --> 04:20.460
Must've been his hero powers.

04:20.460 --> 04:24.170
Or, actually, I think Helck
is just built different somehow.

04:24.750 --> 04:27.830
Our commanding officer and captain
are both dead.

04:27.830 --> 04:30.170
We rank-and-file soldiers
are all that's left now.

04:30.630 --> 04:34.460
Lord Edil, I'm sorry, but there's
just nothing more that we can do...

04:34.460 --> 04:39.130
Our squadron had originally been tasked
with saving Edil's town from invading monsters.

04:39.960 --> 04:41.790
It is what it is.

04:42.960 --> 04:45.210
He was the son of the town's baron.

04:45.210 --> 04:47.460
The soldiers stationed there
were being overwhelmed,

04:47.460 --> 04:52.130
so he traveled to the capital to request that a
monster hunting squadron be dispatched to help.

04:54.460 --> 04:55.460
Dammit...

04:55.460 --> 04:57.170
What am I supposed to do now?

05:02.170 --> 05:03.250
Sir Helck!

05:05.080 --> 05:08.750
I won't be able to do as much
as a full military squadron,

05:09.040 --> 05:13.790
but if you're willing to have me,
then I'll accompany you back to your town.

05:14.460 --> 05:19.080
If there's any chance that I can
save some lives, then I'll gladly do so.

05:19.080 --> 05:20.330
Sir Helck!

05:21.130 --> 05:22.580
Thank you!

05:23.580 --> 05:28.040
Instead of going back to the capital,
I traveled with Edil to his town.

05:29.170 --> 05:30.580
Three days later...

05:31.000 --> 05:32.170
Oh god!

05:32.170 --> 05:35.080
My town! It's on fire!

05:36.630 --> 05:38.250
We were too late.

05:38.250 --> 05:40.080
They couldn't hold out any longer!

05:40.080 --> 05:43.580
Goddammit! Those infernal monsters!
Curse them to Hell!

05:43.580 --> 05:45.500
Edil! There's still a chance!

05:45.710 --> 05:48.330
The town doesn't look like
it's been fully overrun just yet!

05:48.330 --> 05:51.960
I'm willing to bet not much time has past since
the monsters actually breached the defenses!

05:51.960 --> 05:54.330
Edil! Get on your feet!
And prepare to fight!

05:54.330 --> 05:56.170
We have to defend the town!

06:01.420 --> 06:03.880
Hello! Is anybody alive?!

06:07.960 --> 06:10.290
You infernal freaks! You'll pay for this!

06:10.290 --> 06:11.630
Wait, Edil!

06:12.540 --> 06:14.000
I see a survivor!

06:16.210 --> 06:17.670
I guess arrows aren't going to cut it.

06:17.920 --> 06:20.250
Annoying crustacean bastards.

06:21.290 --> 06:22.210
Fine then.

06:22.210 --> 06:23.920
Let's see how you handle a holy sword!

06:34.170 --> 06:36.380
Incredible...
Is she one of the town guards?

06:36.380 --> 06:38.380
No, we don't have any female troops.

06:41.830 --> 06:43.080
I'm Helck.

06:43.080 --> 06:45.500
A soldier here to help fend off
the monster invasion.

06:45.500 --> 06:46.750
A soldier?

06:46.750 --> 06:48.380
Oh jeez! Why are you topless?!

06:49.250 --> 06:50.880
Well, whatever.

06:51.130 --> 06:54.000
I was just thinking this was
going to be difficult to finish solo.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.330
Help me get rid of these monsters,
would you?

07:06.330 --> 07:07.290
Unbelievable.

07:07.290 --> 07:09.750
You defeated so many of them in just one go...

07:09.750 --> 07:11.750
Great! Looks like we're done here.

07:11.750 --> 07:14.500
Whoa, Mr. Topless Trooper!
Wait a darn second!

07:14.500 --> 07:16.420
Hey, nice work out there!

07:16.420 --> 07:18.420
How exactly did you do that just now?!

07:18.420 --> 07:19.210
Huh?

07:19.210 --> 07:20.750
Did I really hear your punch go "kablam"?!

07:20.750 --> 07:23.080
And how did you wipe
out the monsters so easily?!

07:23.080 --> 07:24.290
It's not normal!

07:24.290 --> 07:25.290
Oh?

07:25.290 --> 07:27.380
Well, you were making
short work of them yourself!

07:27.380 --> 07:29.000
That was some fantastic swordsmanship!

07:29.000 --> 07:32.170
Yeah, I am pretty confident
with how I handle a sword.

07:32.170 --> 07:35.630
But in this case, it's probably my blade itself
that makes the biggest difference.

07:36.750 --> 07:39.540
I wield a holy sword that's been passed down
in my family for generations.

07:39.540 --> 07:43.460
Its blade has been infused with a special magic
that's very effective against monsters.

07:43.460 --> 07:44.580
You don't say?

07:44.580 --> 07:46.670
That sounds like a really extraordinary weapon.

07:46.670 --> 07:47.580
Exactly.

07:47.580 --> 07:49.750
There's no other sword like it in the world.

07:49.750 --> 07:52.250
And in the hands of someone
with my level of skill,

07:52.250 --> 07:55.170
it becomes a force more powerful
than any regular soldier.

07:55.290 --> 07:58.380
But you just wiped out more than double
the amount of monsters that I did!

07:58.380 --> 08:01.080
Plus you did it faster!
And with your BARE HANDS!

08:01.080 --> 08:02.250
That's insane!

08:02.250 --> 08:04.250
Do you have some kind of
legendary item or what?!

08:04.250 --> 08:06.710
You gotta tell me!
Who are you, really?!

08:06.830 --> 08:07.880
Helck the soldier!

08:07.880 --> 08:09.420
Yeah, you said that already!

08:09.630 --> 08:11.830
Actually, I used to be a
castle construction worker.

08:11.830 --> 08:12.710
Okay.

08:12.710 --> 08:15.460
So you're just going to play dumb
with me, huh?

08:15.460 --> 08:18.210
Hey! Captain!

08:18.790 --> 08:20.500
Lord Edil!

08:21.080 --> 08:23.130
Thank heavens! So there are survivors!

08:23.630 --> 08:26.290
These brave warriors here saved our lives!

08:26.290 --> 08:29.250
Most of the townspeople have been evacuated
to the mansion grounds.

08:29.500 --> 08:30.500
Oh, I see.

08:30.500 --> 08:32.540
You must be a mercenary group, then.

08:32.540 --> 08:33.710
That's right.

08:33.710 --> 08:36.290
We were just passing by
when we noticed the smoke.

08:36.290 --> 08:37.880
And started fighting before we knew it.

08:38.170 --> 08:40.830
Monsters were the cause
of many disasters back then,

08:40.830 --> 08:42.330
which had given rise

08:42.330 --> 08:45.460
to several mercenary groups who specialized
in exterminating them for money.

08:45.710 --> 08:48.380
The young woman we met was
the leader of one such group,

08:48.380 --> 08:50.290
who told us her name was Alicia.

08:49.540 --> 08:55.330
<b>Mercenary Leader</b>

08:49.540 --> 08:55.330
<b>Alicia</b>

08:50.290 --> 08:53.250
Normally, we sign contracts
before doing any fighting.

08:53.250 --> 08:55.380
But you can consider this one on the house.

08:55.380 --> 08:58.330
Lady Alicia, I can't thank you enough
for what you've done.

08:58.830 --> 09:02.130
Would you be willing to lending us
your aid once more?

09:02.130 --> 09:04.380
The monsters will attack again.

09:04.380 --> 09:06.330
We need more soldiers here!

09:07.710 --> 09:10.330
There's an outbreak of monsters
going on right now.

09:10.330 --> 09:14.460
To be honest, I recommend you abandon this town
and evacuate your people to somewhere safer.

09:15.670 --> 09:16.790
However...

09:17.380 --> 09:19.040
Mr. Topless Trooper.

09:19.040 --> 09:23.170
If you agree to lend a hand, then we might
be strong enough to keep the monsters at bay.

09:23.290 --> 09:26.080
Defeating monsters
is the whole reason I'm here!

09:26.080 --> 09:28.080
I will gladly offer you my assistance.

09:28.080 --> 09:30.130
I'll follow whatever order you give me.

09:30.500 --> 09:31.750
Sir Helck...

09:32.580 --> 09:34.920
Okay! It's a done deal.

09:34.920 --> 09:36.130
Time is of the essence.

09:36.130 --> 09:38.000
We need to start planning
our strategy right away.

09:38.250 --> 09:39.380
Pleasure workin' with ya!

09:39.380 --> 09:40.290
Same here!

09:40.290 --> 09:41.580
Welcome aboard, mate!

09:41.580 --> 09:42.630
Glad to have ya.

09:42.630 --> 09:46.380
And that was how my days
fighting as a mercenary began.

09:51.630 --> 09:53.960
Check it out, Edil! They're huge!

09:53.960 --> 09:55.460
What a bountiful harvest.

09:55.830 --> 09:56.920
Helck!

09:57.500 --> 09:59.250
Monster attack! Prepare for battle!

09:59.250 --> 09:59.960
Right!

09:59.960 --> 10:01.330
I shall join you!

10:01.330 --> 10:03.540
You just keep harvesting the apples, Edil!

10:03.540 --> 10:05.500
Otherwise we won't get it done
by the end of the day!

10:05.500 --> 10:06.710
All right!

10:06.710 --> 10:09.330
Monsters would appear without warning.

10:09.540 --> 10:12.210
Nice! Just look at the char on these babies!

10:12.210 --> 10:13.960
It smells so good.

10:14.130 --> 10:16.250
Helck! More monsters! We gotta go!

10:16.250 --> 10:16.790
Right!

10:16.790 --> 10:17.960
I shall join you!

10:18.130 --> 10:20.170
No way!
The meat will end up burned to a crisp!

10:20.170 --> 10:21.540
Keep rotating it for me!

10:21.540 --> 10:22.630
All right.

10:22.830 --> 10:25.380
They would come when
we were working on the farm,

10:25.380 --> 10:27.420
or when were in the middle of preparing food.

10:27.710 --> 10:29.380
It didn't matter if it was day or night.

10:29.630 --> 10:31.500
Monster attack! Grab your gear!

10:32.420 --> 10:33.630
Monster attack!

10:34.790 --> 10:37.210
There was never any downtime for us
during those days.

10:38.710 --> 10:41.080
Uh... that's not what it sounds like to me.

10:41.880 --> 10:42.960
But it's true!

10:42.960 --> 10:44.790
Everyone was always on pins and needles.

10:44.790 --> 10:45.920
Fair enough.

10:45.920 --> 10:48.750
That makes sense.
Your lives were on the line, after all.

10:49.250 --> 10:51.790
The number of monsters we faced
was astronomical.

10:51.790 --> 10:54.830
Some of them were very menacing,
but nobody ever fled from battle.

10:55.250 --> 10:58.170
The mercenaries who held the line
against the invading monsters

10:58.170 --> 11:01.130
were a bright and jovial bunch,
although they did complain at times.

11:01.540 --> 11:05.420
Edil was a source of inspiration for everyone,
always giving the utmost effort,

11:05.420 --> 11:08.210
and putting the safety of his friends
and people first.

11:08.710 --> 11:10.250
And then there was Alicia,

11:10.250 --> 11:12.580
a highly-skilled fighter who saved us
from a number of tight spots

11:12.580 --> 11:15.630
and never gave up
no matter how bad things looked.

11:16.210 --> 11:18.250
Although those were dark times,

11:18.250 --> 11:20.460
being around people like them
put a smile on my face.

11:21.040 --> 11:22.750
It filled me with optimism,

11:22.750 --> 11:25.790
which enabled me to fight without
being overcome by negative emotions.

11:26.500 --> 11:28.380
They were the best comrades
a guy could ask for.

11:32.130 --> 11:34.710
That was another strenuous battle, huh?

11:34.710 --> 11:35.830
Yeah.

11:36.040 --> 11:38.290
We've taken care of ten of their nests.

11:38.290 --> 11:40.000
Only three more to go now.

11:40.000 --> 11:41.830
Just gotta stay the course.

11:41.830 --> 11:45.210
But I have to say, you really are strong
in every sense of the word.

11:45.210 --> 11:48.750
Your wounds heal over in no time.
How does that even work?

11:48.750 --> 11:51.790
I dunno.
I've just always had a knack for it.

11:51.790 --> 11:53.960
Is that really something
you can have a knack for?

11:54.580 --> 11:57.920
This job runs in my family, you know.
My dad was a mercenary, too.

11:58.540 --> 12:02.080
And in the past, way back before
this kingdom had even been established,

12:02.080 --> 12:06.380
they say my grandfather was a Hero
who fought against the demonkin.

12:06.380 --> 12:08.170
Although, I'm not sure I believe it.

12:08.170 --> 12:10.210
Heroes and demonkin, huh?

12:10.210 --> 12:14.210
You know, I've never really heard anybody
use those words except in fairy tales.

12:14.210 --> 12:18.250
Anyway, the point is,
I come from a long line of warriors.

12:18.250 --> 12:19.960
I was so confident in my talent for fighting,

12:19.960 --> 12:22.880
that I thought there was no man
who could best me.

12:23.420 --> 12:26.420
But now... I realize
there is no limit to excellence.

12:26.420 --> 12:28.420
You're so strong it's crazy.

12:28.420 --> 12:29.130
Huh?

12:29.130 --> 12:31.630
It's actually taken my confidence down a peg.

12:31.630 --> 12:33.040
Oh gosh! Don't say that!

12:33.040 --> 12:35.130
I'm just good at throwing my weight around!

12:35.130 --> 12:37.040
I don't even have the skill
to use bows or swords!

12:37.040 --> 12:38.960
Weapons aren't part of the equation here!

12:39.170 --> 12:42.170
It's just frustrating that my very best
is still weak compared to you!

12:42.830 --> 12:46.000
Besides, I've noticed the way you fight.

12:46.000 --> 12:49.460
You do it with so much ease
that you can also keep an eye out for others.

12:50.710 --> 12:54.960
Meanwhile, it takes all of my focus
just to defeat the monsters in front of me.

12:54.960 --> 12:56.250
No matter how I hard try,

12:56.250 --> 12:58.750
I can never be the pillar of strength
on the battlefield that you are.

12:58.960 --> 13:03.330
Honestly, my pride has been
torn to shreds ever since I met you.

13:03.330 --> 13:04.960
It's so disheartening.

13:06.250 --> 13:07.880
Alicia...

13:07.880 --> 13:10.210
But whatever! Putting that aside...

13:11.080 --> 13:13.040
You're absolutely amazing!

13:13.040 --> 13:16.330
I just know you have what it takes
to save an even greater number of people.

13:17.130 --> 13:20.420
Your strength and caring heart
make me sure of it.

13:22.130 --> 13:23.670
Even as strong as I am,

13:23.670 --> 13:26.960
there were still some people
who I couldn't manage to save.

13:27.460 --> 13:31.080
But you're different,
I know you could save them all.

13:32.040 --> 13:35.500
Our little band of mercenaries
wouldn't have made it this far without you.

13:35.500 --> 13:38.580
I'm almost certain most of us
would have died along the way.

13:38.580 --> 13:41.250
So I can't thank you enough, Helck.

13:41.960 --> 13:43.630
After the town is safe,

13:43.630 --> 13:46.960
you should know I'm not letting you go back
to being a construction worker or a soldier!

13:49.500 --> 13:52.040
I hope that you'll continue
to fight by our side!

13:54.290 --> 13:56.250
Roger that! Captain!

13:58.500 --> 14:00.330
Hey. Helck?

14:01.170 --> 14:03.630
Sorry. I was just spacing out.

14:06.170 --> 14:07.500
Ultimately,

14:07.500 --> 14:11.420
I continued to hunt monsters alongside Alicia
and her mercenaries after that.

14:12.080 --> 14:13.630
It went on for about four years.

14:13.630 --> 14:15.790
We just kept fighting relentlessly.

14:16.460 --> 14:19.460
But in spite of that, the number of monsters
never diminished.

14:19.460 --> 14:21.330
They only continued to cause more harm.

14:21.920 --> 14:23.750
In the midst of these dark times,

14:23.750 --> 14:28.540
the kingdom made an announcement that brought
some rays of hope back into people's lives.

14:29.710 --> 14:32.830
There is a land of death to the west
known as the Demon Realm!

14:32.830 --> 14:33.960
A recent expedition there

14:33.960 --> 14:37.330
has revealed the location of the
Demon Lord's castle spoken of in ancient texts!

14:37.500 --> 14:39.960
The Demon Lord is the root of all evil!

14:39.960 --> 14:42.080
We can stop the plague of monsters
by defeating him!

14:42.290 --> 14:43.540
I hereby announce...

14:43.540 --> 14:45.960
that we will dispatch a force to kill him!

14:47.670 --> 14:48.750
That's wrong.

14:48.750 --> 14:50.250
We weren't the ones responsible

14:50.250 --> 14:53.500
for spawning those monsters and
sending them to the human realm.

14:53.500 --> 14:58.040
Not long after, the Human King called upon
a single warrior to fulfill that mission.

14:58.670 --> 15:03.880
There is no one with the strength necessary to
bring down the Demon Lord Thor except for you.

15:03.880 --> 15:06.750
Failure is not an option.
You must kill the Demon Lord.

15:07.000 --> 15:09.460
Go see it done! Cless the Hero!

15:09.460 --> 15:11.920
Restore peace to the world!

15:12.380 --> 15:16.210
And so, Cless left on a journey
to defeat the Demon Lord.

15:17.630 --> 15:18.540
Sir Helck.

15:18.540 --> 15:21.040
Are you sure you don't need
to go see your brother off?

15:21.750 --> 15:22.630
Yeah.

15:23.130 --> 15:25.960
My top priority is keeping this area safe.

15:26.080 --> 15:28.210
You must be worried about your little bro.

15:28.210 --> 15:30.750
I mean, he'll be fighting against
something way worse than monsters.

15:30.750 --> 15:33.080
It's the king of the monsters,
the Demon Lord himself!

15:33.540 --> 15:35.830
Yeah, but we're talking about Cless the Hero!

15:35.830 --> 15:39.250
He's so crazy strong that people call him
the second coming of the legendary hero!

15:39.250 --> 15:40.210
Should be a cakewalk!

15:40.210 --> 15:43.210
Except I'm pretty sure just reaching
the Demon Lord is its own ordeal.

15:43.210 --> 15:46.710
He's in an impregnatable fortress guarded
by tens of thousands of demons, after all.

15:46.710 --> 15:50.580
Not to mention, the Demon Lord is supposed
to be just as strong as the legendary hero was.

15:50.580 --> 15:51.670
Can we really win?

15:53.580 --> 15:56.790
Cless will be accompanied by
the heavy infantry commander, Zeruzeon,

15:56.790 --> 15:58.500
the Great Sage, Mikaros,

15:58.500 --> 16:01.920
and a handful of other
battle-hardened warriors.

16:01.920 --> 16:06.040
Plus, I heard that they've assembled a force
of 5,000 highly-trained soldiers at the fort.

16:06.210 --> 16:09.580
Well, if a team like that can't win,
then humanity is just doomed.

16:09.580 --> 16:10.580
For sure.

16:10.580 --> 16:11.500
Jeez!

16:11.500 --> 16:13.830
Don't you guys know
when to keep your mouths shut?!

16:13.830 --> 16:15.790
Have a bit of sympathy, dammit!

16:19.040 --> 16:20.210
Sorry, man.

16:20.210 --> 16:22.500
I know your little brother's life
is riding on all this...

16:22.500 --> 16:23.920
It's okay, don't apologize.

16:24.380 --> 16:26.380
Cless is going to win.

16:26.380 --> 16:27.960
I'm sure of it.

16:29.080 --> 16:32.330
Cless definitely has what it takes
to defeat the Demon Lord

16:32.330 --> 16:34.920
and bring peace to the world for us.

16:39.170 --> 16:44.540
It was three weeks later when we got word
that Cless really had defeated the Demon Lord.

16:48.170 --> 16:49.460
After a deadly struggle,

16:49.460 --> 16:52.210
Cless managed to pierce his blade
through the Demon Lord's forehead,

16:52.210 --> 16:53.960
and put him down for good.

16:54.750 --> 16:57.250
The epic tale spread through
the populace like wildfire.

16:58.330 --> 17:00.460
A new era of peace was ushered in.

17:01.250 --> 17:04.040
People filled the streets
of towns and cities in celebration.

17:04.920 --> 17:06.000
However,

17:06.000 --> 17:08.920
I wasn't in any position to celebrate.

17:09.580 --> 17:10.580
Because...

17:10.830 --> 17:12.040
Cless!

17:12.580 --> 17:13.670
Helck.

17:18.500 --> 17:20.960
He managed to survive the worst of it,

17:20.960 --> 17:23.580
but I'm sorry to say
that he remains in critical condition.

17:26.500 --> 17:27.540
Cless...

17:28.130 --> 17:29.630
You did a great job.

17:29.630 --> 17:31.540
But you can't die on me now.

17:31.540 --> 17:33.040
As your big brother,

17:33.040 --> 17:35.210
I just won't stand for it, okay?

17:40.040 --> 17:41.420
Helck...

17:43.040 --> 17:45.290
It's all right. Don't cry.

17:45.500 --> 17:47.750
Cless will be back on his feet
before you know it.

17:48.000 --> 17:51.290
The battle against the Demon Lord
had gravely injured Cless,

17:51.290 --> 17:54.420
and left his body ravaged by a poison
of unknown origin.

17:54.420 --> 17:55.540
Helck.

17:55.540 --> 17:57.960
Do you happen to remember me?

17:59.380 --> 18:01.290
You're the doctor who helped us!

18:01.880 --> 18:03.460
I hardly recognized you.

18:03.460 --> 18:06.250
You're no longer the little boy I met,
but a strapping young warrior.

18:06.250 --> 18:08.380
This is Mikaros the Great Sage.

18:08.380 --> 18:11.960
He was one of the people who fought
alongside Cless on this recent campaign.

18:11.960 --> 18:14.540
I had no idea that you were
the Great Sage, sir.

18:14.920 --> 18:16.960
It's no more than a title.

18:16.960 --> 18:18.790
Although I joined the campaign,

18:18.790 --> 18:21.380
I was practically worthless when
it came time to take down the Demon Lord.

18:22.040 --> 18:25.670
Their battle was more ferocious
than anything I had imagined.

18:25.670 --> 18:28.830
They were fighting on a level that far
surpassed what the rest of us were capable of.

18:28.830 --> 18:33.710
The best we could do was keep ourselves safe,
so that we didn't hold Cless back.

18:34.210 --> 18:35.420
I'm sorry.

18:35.420 --> 18:39.540
Cless wouldn't have been so gravely injured
if we had been just a little stronger.

18:39.790 --> 18:43.630
All the same, Cless never would have
made it back alive without their help.

18:43.630 --> 18:45.420
Please don't bear a grudge against them.

18:45.420 --> 18:48.000
Of course.
I would never do something like that.

18:48.210 --> 18:52.580
Cless expended the very last of his strength
and brought down the Demon Lord for us.

18:52.580 --> 18:55.710
His brave efforts
have guaranteed us all a future.

18:56.000 --> 18:58.290
Letting him die is out of the question.

18:58.290 --> 18:59.750
I've cured him once before.

18:59.750 --> 19:01.710
And I guarantee that I will find a way
to do it again.

19:02.210 --> 19:03.670
You have my word.

19:04.460 --> 19:07.210
Please and thank you.

19:09.580 --> 19:11.710
Everyone is having a wild time out there.

19:11.710 --> 19:14.630
Even though the hero who saved the kingdom
is in such a precarious situation...

19:14.630 --> 19:15.880
You can hardly blame them.

19:15.880 --> 19:18.250
Peace has finally come
after so much suffering.

19:18.250 --> 19:20.000
Do you really think so?

19:20.000 --> 19:22.880
I mean, monsters are still appearing
just like they were before.

19:22.880 --> 19:25.420
It honestly doesn't feel like
anything has changed to me.

19:25.420 --> 19:28.000
It's probably just a few survivors
that were left in the nests.

19:28.000 --> 19:29.380
They'll be snuffed out in due time.

19:29.630 --> 19:31.420
I hope that's all it is...

19:32.330 --> 19:34.710
C'mon, Captain! You gotta stay positive!

19:34.710 --> 19:35.790
Yeah!

19:35.790 --> 19:37.960
Sorry! You're right!

19:37.960 --> 19:41.210
Unfortunately, it turned out Alicia's concerns
were right on the money.

19:44.750 --> 19:47.210
Hey, wake up! Something's wrong!

19:47.210 --> 19:50.290
M-monsters are coming!
A massive hoard of them!

19:50.290 --> 19:52.750
W-we gotta get word to the capital!

19:55.210 --> 19:57.250
Everybody evacuate! Get to the castle!

19:57.250 --> 19:58.710
What the hell is happening?!

19:58.710 --> 20:00.210
Protect us from the monsters!

20:00.420 --> 20:01.830
What has gotten into them?

20:01.830 --> 20:04.000
The monster attack has
thrown everyone into a panic,

20:04.000 --> 20:06.170
because they were convinced
the fighting was over.

20:06.170 --> 20:08.420
I thought that you guys killed the Demon Lord!

20:08.420 --> 20:11.000
Tell the truth!
You just ran away from him, didn't you?!

20:11.000 --> 20:12.250
Watch your mouth!

20:12.250 --> 20:14.210
I saw the Demon Lord perish
with my own two eyes!

20:14.210 --> 20:16.210
Then why the hell are monsters
still attacking us?!

20:16.210 --> 20:18.170
Quit feeding us your bullshit!

20:19.170 --> 20:21.920
It won't be long until the monsters
break through the castle walls!

20:21.920 --> 20:23.210
Sir Cless!

20:23.210 --> 20:25.040
Where's Cless?! Get Cless out here!

20:25.040 --> 20:27.540
That's not an option!
Cless has been severely injured!

20:27.540 --> 20:29.210
He's not in any shape to fight!

20:29.210 --> 20:31.420
That's a load of crap! You damn cowards!

20:31.420 --> 20:33.040
What else is a hero good for?!

20:33.040 --> 20:34.540
Get out here, Cless!

20:34.540 --> 20:36.750
You can't just leave us to die here!

20:36.750 --> 20:39.000
Sir Cless! Please save us!

20:39.000 --> 20:40.960
Come fight, you chicken shit!

20:41.880 --> 20:43.750
I can't believe what I'm hearing right now.

20:43.750 --> 20:46.330
How can they act like this when
they know Sir Cless is injured?

20:46.580 --> 20:47.630
Helck.

20:47.630 --> 20:49.830
I'm sure you're tempted to give them
a piece of your mind,

20:49.830 --> 20:51.330
but we need to protect the capital.

20:51.330 --> 20:53.540
It would be catastrophically bad
if this place falls to the monsters.

20:53.540 --> 20:54.670
Alicia.

20:54.670 --> 20:57.000
You said the hoard of monsters
is coming from the direction

20:57.000 --> 20:58.420
of the Demon Lord's castle, right?

20:58.420 --> 21:00.000
Uh, yeah.

21:00.000 --> 21:02.670
I don't get the impression
that those guys are lying.

21:02.670 --> 21:04.330
The Demon Lord is formidable.

21:04.330 --> 21:07.790
It's entirely possible that he found some way
to revive himself after being killed.

21:07.960 --> 21:09.080
Wait a second!

21:09.380 --> 21:11.080
Don't get any crazy ideas!

21:12.920 --> 21:15.880
I'm gonna go defeat the Demon Lord.

21:24.250 --> 21:27.880
Nee, bokura ga egaiteita yume wa nandakke

21:27.880 --> 21:31.080
Nee, bokura ga egaiteita yume wa nandakke

21:31.710 --> 21:35.670
Chiisakute doro darake demo daiji na omoide

21:35.670 --> 21:39.080
Chiisakute doro darake demo daiji na omoide

21:39.830 --> 21:43.540
Migi mo hidari mo wakaranai bukakkou na boku no

21:43.540 --> 21:46.630
Migi mo hidari mo wakaranai bukakkou na boku no

21:47.580 --> 21:54.500
Te o hiite tasukete kureta suzushii manazashi

21:55.580 --> 21:59.460
Daijoubu daijoubutte iinagara

21:59.460 --> 22:03.380
Kimi wa nando mo boku o dakishimeta

22:03.380 --> 22:06.750
Atatakai kono te o kondo wa boku ga nigirunda

22:06.750 --> 22:09.960
Atatakai kono te o kondo wa boku ga nigirunda

22:11.210 --> 22:18.380
Kimi no namae o sakenda sekai wa waratta

22:18.670 --> 22:22.630
Tsunagi tomeru sono kotoba ga nani yori toutoi

22:22.630 --> 22:25.750
Tsunagi tomeru sono kotoba ga nani yori toutoi

22:26.880 --> 22:34.080
Kore ga bokura no unmei naraba nurikaeyou

22:34.330 --> 22:38.330
Kurayami no sono mukou gawa

22:38.330 --> 22:45.330
Tomo ni tsukamaeru hikari

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>The Power of Heroes</b>

22:46.830 --> 22:49.750
